FORMAT: 1A
HOST: https://dashboard.timing.tech/timingapi.svc

# Timing






## Scheduling Request [/scheduling/account/{account}]

+ Parameters
    + account (String, Required) - Token

### Request [POST]
<b>Request for the most efficient scheduling and dispatching options based on traffic conditions,
skills type and level, constraints, analytics and AI. The request is asynchronous. To get the results use 'Scheduling Get' API method. Timing can also 'Push' the result by given URI.</b>




* callId (String, Required): Call Identifier
* address (String, Required if geolocation omitted): Appointment address
* city (String, Required): Appointment city
* geolocation (String, Required if address omitted): Appointment geolocation 
* hasNewAddress (Bool, Required): Set to true in case the customer already exist and his address was changed. Default = false.
* territoryId (String): Territory identifier. Send NULL if workforce has no territories.
* taskIds (String, Required): Task IDs separated by comma
* skills (Array of objects) - Array of skills (id & level) which required to handle the job. The less expensive resource will be preffered
* parts (Array) - The parts that required to complete the tasks on the customer site.
* priorityLevel (Number) - Determine the priority level of the appointment (1/10/100/1000). 1000 = highest priority. High priority customers will push lower priority customers on the timeline. Also, high priority customers will not be delayed by lower priorities
* estimatedAccessTime (Number): Estimated access time in minutes from arrival to address until coming to the site
* planningHorizon (Number, Required): Planning horizon in business days. <br> '0'=on demand (same business day)
* timeWindows (String Array): Time window array of prefered windows to schedule the appointment. Required format - yyyyMMddHHmm 
* overrideServiceTime (Number): By this field it is possible to override the estimated service time and provide a new estimation for this specific job
* dependenceCalls (String Array): An array of calls which should be attended before current scheduling request. 
* techId (String): Technician identifier. In case exists indicates of preferred technician
* timezone (Number, Required): GMT value in minutes



+ Request (application/json)

        {
           
            "callId": "123123",
            "address": "Manhattan Avenue, New York, NY, USA",
            "city": "New York",
            "geolocation": "40.808860,-73.954030",
            "hasNewAddress": false,
            "territoryId": null,
            "taskIds": "674,369,975",
            "skills": [{"Id":1, "level":1},{"Id":1, "level":2}],
            "parts": ["243738", "5657494", "6856353"],
            "priorityLevel": 1,
            "estimatedAccessTime" : 10,
            "planningHorizon": "7",
            "timeWindows": [{"startTimeWindow":"201903011000","endTimeWindow":"201903011200"},{"startTimeWindow":"201903021000","endTimeWindow":"201903021200"}],
            "overrideServiceTime": null,
            "timeWindowflexibility":1, 
            "dependenceCalls": ["2423453","34534645"],
            "techId": "123214",
            "timezone": "-240",
           
        }
        
+ Response 200 (application/json)

    + Body
    
            {
                "code": 1000,
                "message": "OK",
                "description": null,
                "result" : "Processing..."
            }  
            
