                }
            } 
            



## Scheduling Force [/schedulingForce/account/{account}]

+ Parameters
    + account (String, Required) - Token
    
### Create [POST]

<b>Create a new appointment by scheduling enforcment </b>

* callId (String, Required) - Call identifier
* companyName (String) - The name of the cusomer's company
* customerId (String, Required) - Customer identifier
* firstName (String, Required) - First name
* lastName (String, Required) - Last name (surename)
* mobile (String, Required) - Phones list separated by comma. The first is the primary
* address (String, Required if geolocation is empty) - Customer's address
* city (String, Required if geolocation is empty) - Customer's city
* geolocation (String , Required if address & city are empty) - Customer's geolocation
* customerTypeId (Number, Required) - Customer's type
* territoryId (String, Required) - Customer's territory ID
* taskIds (String, Required) - Tasks list separated by comma
* skills (Object array, Required) - Skills object array
* estimatedAccessTime (Number) - Estimated access time from enter to the Customer's building and untill starting handling the tasks in minutes. Default = 0
* overrideServiceTime (Number): By this field it is possible to override the estimated service time and provide a new estimation
* priorityLevel (Number) - defined the appointment priority, 1/10/100/1000 when 1 = regular priorty and 1000 = highest priority
* techId (String, Required) - Technician identifier
* customerJobDescription (String) - Customer's description
* dispatcherJobDescription (String) - Dispatcher's description
* techJobDescription (String) - Technician's description
* jobStatus (String) - Job status description
* openerName (String) - The representative who set the appointment
* serviceTypeId (Number, Required) - Service type
* startTimeWindow (String, Required) - Start time window in yyyyMMddHHmm format
* endTimeWindow (String, Required) -  End time window in yyyyMMddHHmm format
* positionOnRoute (Number, Required) - Indicated the dervice call order in the route (i.e to the third appointment on the route -> =3)
* validatePosition (Boolean) - If true (recommanded), the system will validate the position. Default = false
* timezone (Number, Required) - The timezone account in minutes
* product (Object) - customer's product 
* id (String) - product identifier
* model (String) - product model
* productNumber (String) - product number
* serialNumber (String, Reqiured) - product serial number
* purchaseDate (String) - prduct purchase date yyyyMMdd
* warrantyExpiry (String) - product warranty expiration
* insuranceExpiry (String) - product insuarnce expiration
* installerName (String) - The person full name who install the product
* installerMobile (String) - The person mobile who install the product
* customerOverrideType(Number, Required) - 0 = None; 1 = Details; 2 = Address; 3 = Both. Default is 0
* driveUrl (String): Link to related files


+ Request (application/json) 

        {
           
            "callId": "123123",
            "companyName": "HP",
            "customerId":"67554735",
            "firstName": "Bill",
            "lastName": "Evans",
            "mobile": "+12025550142, +12025555179",
            "address": "Manhattan Avenue, New York, NY, USA", 
